Clone, fetch and push a repository with its own GIT_TOKEN variable, and list it
in the repository picker.

A repository whose variables (omnigent_repo_env) include GIT_TOKEN is cloned
with that token instead of the user's GitHub App token, and its checkout keeps
using it: the workspace-prep init container now mounts the repositories'
variables Secrets too, and omnigent_repo_env.clone_command writes a
repository-local credential helper that reads the mounted token file. The
GitHub picker routes add those repositories to the App's list and list their
branches with the token (omnigent_repo_env_api).
Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f), after 0001-0009.

